	<section_number>15.2-1911</section_number>
	<catch_line>Statement by defendant precludes appeal</catch_line>
	<text>
		If a statement, as provided for in § 15.2-1910, is filed by each defendant, no appeal or writ of error shall thereafter be allowed such defendant.
	</text>
	<history>1938, p. 49; Michie Code 1942, § 4387a; Code 1950, § 25-50; 2003, c. 940.</history>
